{"summary":"Fixed the ascii.qdp reader in astropy/io/ascii/qdp.py, which assumed QDP commands are upper case and crashed on hand-written files like "read serr 1 2" with "ValueError: Unrecognized QDP line". Root cause: _line_type compiled its line-classification regex (command "READ [TS]ERR", new-table "NO NO", data tokens) case-sensitively. Fix: compile the regex with flags=re.IGNORECASE so all QDP line types match regardless of case, and make the masked-value check in _get_tables_from_qdp_file case-insensitive (v.upper() == "NO") so lowercase "no" data values are masked rather than failing float() conversion. Also added a doctest documenting lowercase command acceptance. Verified with the exact reproduction from the PR description (now reads a table with col1, col1_err, col2, col2_err), edge cases (mixed-case commands, lowercase NO values, lowercase new-table marker, comma-delimited files via sep=',', gibberish still rejected), the existing test_qdp.py suite (8 passed), qdp.py module doctests (4 passed), and the full astropy/io/ascii/tests suite (825 passed, 36 skipped, 6 xfailed). Only the source file was modified; no test or config files were touched.","final_verification":{"checks": ["cd /testbed && printf 'read serr 1 2\n1 0.5 1 0.5\n' > /tmp/test.qdp && python -c "import warnings; from astropy.table import Table; warnings.simplefilter('ignore'); t = Table.read('/tmp/test.qdp', format='ascii.qdp'); assert t.colnames == ['col1', 'col1_err', 'col2', 'col2_err'], t.colnames; assert t['col1_err'][0] == 0.5 and t['col2_err'][0] == 0.5; print('reproduction reads with errors:', t.colnames)"", "cd /testbed && python -c "from astropy.io.ascii.qdp import _line_type; assert _line_type('read serr 1 2') == 'command'; assert _line_type('Read TERR 3') == 'command'; assert _line_type('no no no') == 'new'; assert _line_type('1 no') == 'data,2'; [_line_type(b) is None for b in []];
import contextlib
for bad in ['read serrx 1', 'N O N NOON OON O', 'gibberish']:
    try:
        _line_type(bad)
    except ValueError:
        pass
    else:
        raise SystemExit(bad + ' should be rejected')
print('case-insensitive matching + rejection checks OK')"", "cd /testbed && python -m pytest astropy/io/ascii/tests/test_qdp.py -q --no-header -p no:cacheprovider", "cd /testbed && python -m pytest --doctest-modules astropy/io/ascii/qdp.py -q --no-header -p no:cacheprovider", "cd /testbed && python -m pytest astropy/io/ascii/tests -q --no-header -p no:cacheprovider 2>&1 | tail -1"]}}

